sub1:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-overall> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Gemini 4 Argon (MorphoEval Loop 054 Pass 1 Assessor)" ;
        dcterms:identifier "gemini-4-argon" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf orcid:0009-0007-4948-9192 ;
        foaf:homepage <https://deepmind.google> .

    <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Menshykau & Iber (2013), Zubkov et al. (2015) & Watanabe & Costantini (2004) kidney ureteric bud GDNF-RET-Wnt11 Turing branching morphogenesis — MorphoEval overall 47.8/100" ;
        dcterms:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
        dcterms:description "Pass 1 (v1 baseline) evaluation of `2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py` (52.4/100). The v1 script computes the homogeneous steady state (R*, G*) = (a + b, b / (a + b)^2) and linearized Turing dispersion curve of the Menshykau & Iber (2013) Schnakenberg-type GDNF-RET reaction-diffusion system, integrates a 1D ampulla arc profile, and draws a purely geometric symmetric binary tree. However, v1 omits dichotomous vs trichotomous tip-splitting mode selection across normalized tip radius R_tip / lambda_c, omits 2D self-avoiding ureteric tree growth driven by local mesenchymal GDNF consumption sinks (-gamma R^2 G), omits Spry1-/- hyper-branching, exogenous GDNF bead supernumerary budding, and Gdnf+/- or PRR^(UB-/-) hypoplasia controls, neither loads nor verifies `datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret_reference.json`, and performs zero biological specimen segmentation on `datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/kidney_ureteric_tree_specimen.jpg`. Overall 47.8/100 (faithfulness 41.0, reproducibility 63.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 8871db0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 58, Morphological realism / specimen match 22, Parameter expressivity 44, Morphometric validation 48, Source and data traceability 58, Code-to-model traceability 64, Reproducibility package 68. Output judged: docs/media/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret_comparison.png: rendered output of 2012-menshykau-fgf10-shh-lung-turing.py at 8871db0, image/png, 134295 B, 1890×616 px, artifact_sha256 b5e314ac269c2f687641e61f84f770113eafd6fd8b1ca184f99bb3e0769aabe8 (sha256 b5e314ac269c2f687641e61f84f770113eafd6fd8b1ca184f99bb3e0769aabe8), spec_fingerprint 98ff66f09006e3949d0b868aa475a2ba217b732f0d29cc82d9a5d3b4965aeb50. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 98ff66f09006e3949d0b868aa475a2ba217b732f0d29cc82d9a5d3b4965aeb50; artifact_sha256: b5e314ac269c2f687641e61f84f770113eafd6fd8b1ca184f99bb3e0769aabe8; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret_reference.json=89257794ab9d8d23..., datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/kidney_ureteric_tree_specimen.jpg=3264f509ba3a6686..., datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/paper_citations.bib=bb8e3d5a5c8877bd..., datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/scout_manifest.json=c55304eda64bfba4...}." ;
        dcterms:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Expand `--self-test`, CLI parameter flags (`--a-ret`, `--b-gdnf`, `--gamma`, `--d-ratio`, `--generations`, `--seed`), and `measure_morphoeval()` to report >= 8 quantitative metrics with reference values, dispersion (RMSE, Pearson r, CV), and negative-control ablation deltas.",
            "remediation needed: Implement a 2D self-avoiding ureteric tree branching simulator coupled to a 2D mesenchymal GDNF diffusion-consumption PDE field (where growing tips consume local GDNF via -gamma*R^2*G and steer up-gradient while mutually repelling via GDNF sink depletion), and simulate all 4 experimental regimes: Wild-Type control, Gdnf+/- or PRR^(UB-/-) hypoplasia, Spry1-/- hyper-branching (Basson et al. 2005), and exogenous GDNF-soaked bead ectopic budding.",
            "remediation needed: Implement semi-implicit (IMEX) Schnakenberg GDNF-RET reaction-diffusion solver across ureteric bud ampulla radii R_tip to demonstrate the exact transition from single-peak elongation (rho_tip < 1.5) to canonical dichotomous tip splitting (1.5 <= rho_tip < 2.5, m = 2 lateral R^2*G hotspots with apical cleft) and trichotomous trifurcation (rho_tip >= 2.5, m = 3 hotspots).",
            "remediation needed: Load and SHA-256-verify `datasets/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret/kidney_ureteric_bud_gdnf_ret_reference.json` and `kidney_ureteric_tree_specimen.jpg` at runtime, segment the E12.5 mouse metanephros whole-mount GFP ureteric bud trees in Panel A (wild-type control, 12 tips) and Panel B (hypoplastic mutant, 6 tips) plus pErk1/2 immunofluorescence intensity in Panels D-I, and extract medial-axis skeleton length, terminal tip counts, and WT-to-mutant tip ratio." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.478"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .
}

